id=a52sxq_e2e_optout_list
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: edge-to-edge opt-out list (Instagram black status bar)
author=kusti420
description=Android 16+ enforces edge-to-edge for apps targeting SDK 36 and ignores their windowOptOutEdgeToEdgeEnforcement; Instagram then draws a black strip under the status bar on its light UI (same on Pixels). Stock One UI hides this with a per-app "force opt-out of edge-to-edge" list (CoreRune FW_FORCE_OPT_OUT_EDGE_TO_EDGE, ActivityTaskManagerServiceExt.mForceOptOutEdgeToEdge) that SCPM downloads into /data/system/packageconfiguration - which never arrives on this port (verified 2026-11-01: the directory does not exist). This ships the list in /system/etc/k4/force_opt_out_e2e.txt and makes both readers of the stock list (WindowManagerService.isEdgeToEdgeDisabled and the ActivityRecord constructor) call com.k4.e2e.K4E2E.contains(list, pkg) = stock list OR the shipped file. 9.3.97-9.3.99 fed the list through `cmd window force-opt-out-e2e-add` at boot instead, but that list is a PackageSpecialManagementList of SCPM's FoldablePackagePolicy group, cleared and refilled ~40 s after boot (and on every refresh), so the entry was gone a minute after boot (race review 2026-11-02, `service call window 70 s16 com.instagram.android` = false). Tester report: "In Instagram the status bar turns black". Verify: well after boot (>2 min), `service call window 70 s16 com.instagram.android` returns 1 and Instagram (light theme) shows a white status bar.
